# Auto commit and push

When you finish work in this repo (implementation, fixes, docs, config):

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to confirm what changed.
2. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
3. Stage relevant files, commit with a concise message focused on **why**, and push to the current branch.
4. Skip commit/push only when the prompt was question-only (no file changes) or the user explicitly says not to.

Follow the git safety protocol: no force push to main, no `--no-verify`, no amend unless allowed.

After pushing, briefly tell the user the commit hash and that it was pushed.
